  "name": "Contractors by metro: roofing, HVAC, plumbing and electrical owners into a campaign",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Contractors by metro: roofing, HVAC, plumbing and electrical owners into a campaign\n\n### How it works\nWork one region at a time with a steady weekly rhythm. Every Monday the workflow splits the metros in Settings (for example Austin, Texas; Denver, Colorado) and, for each, counts owners, founders and partners at construction companies whose description matches your trades (roofing, HVAC, plumbing, electrical) within the radius. Metros within max_per_metro are saved as a list, which joins your campaign once it has filled; larger ones are only reported, so you can narrow them. Slack gets one line per metro. Contractors already in the campaign are not added twice.\n\nCosts: free until a list is added, then 1 credit per new person.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Set metros, radius_miles, trades and max_per_metro in **Settings**.\n4. Pick the campaign in **Add the metro list** and the channel in **Weekly summary**, then activate.\n\n### Customization\nUse one campaign per trade by duplicating the branch with different keywords.",
        "height": 653,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
